AI summary of fixes [modified by ebuild maintainer]:

From: Orson Teodoro
Subject: [PATCH] rtw88: fix 30+ day -110 storm, NULL deref in restart_work and 127dBm wedge
rtw88_8821cu 2-5:1.0 fails after 10-30 days uptime with:
  read register 0xaa failed with -110
  rtw_usb_reg_sec: reg 0x4e0, usb write 1 fail, status: -110
  read register 0x770 failed with -110
Followed by 70s spam and then deadlock on modprobe -rf and
google-chrome hang with:
  firmware crash, start reset and recover
  WARNING: at __flush_workqueue
  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000000
  __flush_workqueue+0x359
  ieee80211_restart_work+0x1b
  note: kworker/0:2 exited with irqs disabled
Root causes:
1) mac80211: AP <redacted> advertises country IE max power
   127 dBm (127 - 0). 127 is invalid (means no limit). Programming
   it wedges RF, leading to 0x770 -110.
2) rtw88 usb: -110 only handled in TX path, not in rtw_usb_read,
   rtw_usb_write, rtw_usb_reg_sec. Device keeps hammering 0x4e0
   after failure, fail_count never checked, causing storm.
3) rtw_usb_tx_agg_skb: ieee80211_purge_tx_queue called while
   holding usb_lock / with fw_recovery holding mutex, causing
   modprobe -rf EBUSY.
4) rtw_fw_recovery_work: Calling usb_reset_device() from inside
   fw_recovery_work that then calls ieee80211_restart_hw() on a
   device that has just disconnected (USB disconnect, device number
   2 -> new device 3). usb_reset fails with descriptor read -110 x4,
   device not accepting address, then restart_work self-flushes its
   own workqueue -> WARN + NULL deref + irqs disabled -> system
   deadlock seen as google-chrome hang.
Fix:
* mac80211: Ignore chan_pwr == 127 or >30 in
  ieee80211_handle_pwr_constr.
* rtw88 usb: Add rtwdev->fail + fail_count, add rtw_usb_mark_fail(),
  check fail in all control paths (read/write/reg_sec/read32/
  write32/write_data/tx_agg), stop IO after 3x -110.
* rtw88 usb: Fix tx_agg to splice tx_ack_queue before purge outside lock.
* rtw88 core: In fw_recovery_work, do usb_reset_device outside mutex,
  check ret == -ENODEV, and abort ieee80211_restart_hw if device gone
  after reset. Prevents self-flush deadlock and chrome hang. Reset
  re-enumeration as 1-5 is expected after failed reset (EHCI->OHCI
  fallback).

